Consider the following two-dimensional array D in C, stored in row-major order:

```c
int D[128][128];
```

Demand paging is used, and each physical page frame holds 512 elements of D. The LRU page-replacement policy is used, and 30 physical page frames are allocated to the process. The process executes:

```c
for (int i = 0; i < 128; i++) {
    for (int j = 0; j < 128; j++) {
        D[j][i] *= 10;
    }
}
```

How many page faults are generated during execution?
